  "interpretation": [
    "Both implementations have two logical stages and the same AOT call counts. The candidate emits A/F in one invocation without a fields-only third call.",
    "Actual selected/primary MTF regions only cover new light rows; each final F row is generated once. U/horizontal scratch and per-call box tables may repeat.",
    "Three observed medians are lower and HP5 UHD is about 3.2% higher. Device peak decreases for both HD cases but increases for both UHD cases.",
    "Portra UHD candidate max thermal state is 0 and control is 1. One pair per case and known background timing drift prevent stable causal speedup claims; Docker remained running.",
    "The comparison is against matching-source E2, not current upstream R. Frozen R is the pixel oracle; old R timing is not mixed into this report.",
    "New persistent F payload is additional to E2. Actual total peaks, process footprint and retention include A/F, scratch, tables, input/output, LUT and pool.",
    "Default release build and 18 targeted Swift tests pass. This does not complete full current-source release AOT/parity or broader JIT/render tests."
  ],
